// Implements [LEX-STATEMENT-BREAK] negative test.
//
// Two statements cannot share a line, because nothing would separate them.
// This is the sibling of `statement_break_juxtaposition.ospo`: there the
// greedy parse invented an application, here it would have to invent a
// boundary. A separate file because the parser reports the FIRST syntax error
// and stops, so a second case in one source pins nothing.

print("a") print("b")
